course: dictionary
lesson: 2141
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around them, tells you which meaning is right. The word «cop» is a good example. «The cop walked down the street» means a police officer, but «You'll cop it for that!» means you will receive something bad.
explain: Look at the clues. If the sentence is about police, crime or trouble, cop probably means police officer or get into trouble. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Slang is casual, everyday talk, and its phrases do not always mean what the words say. «Not much cop» means not very good, not that someone is a police officer. «Fair cop» is British slang for admitting you were caught out fairly.
fact: Cop can be a noun (a cop is a police officer) or a verb (to cop something is to get or receive it).
fact: «Cop» meaning police officer is informal, so it is fine in stories and everyday talk but not in formal writing.
fact: «You'll cop it for that!» means you will get into trouble.
fact: «Cop a look at this» means take a quick look.
fact: «Not much cop» means not very good.
exercise: «The cop helped the lost boy find his mum.» What is a cop here? | A type of sweet | A shop worker | *A police officer | A kind of bird
exercise: «You'll cop it for that!» What does cop it mean? | To win a prize | To be very happy | *To get into trouble | To go to sleep
exercise: «Cop a look at this» means which action? | Cook a meal | Shout loudly | *Take a quick look | Run away fast
test: Tom says, «That film was not much cop.» What does he mean? | It was a very long film | It was in colour | It had a police officer in it | *It was not very good
test: «He had to cop to the broken window.» What does cop to mean? | To hide it | *To admit it | To paint it | To clean it
exam: Read this: «Fair cop, I was caught.» What does fair cop mean? | A fair price at the shop | *Admitting you were caught out fairly | Winning a fair game | A police officer who is kind
